PRIME CAYLEY TELESCOPE: PROD Q(1/p_k) = PROD (p_k+1)/(p_k-1)
============================================================

  PROD up to p=  2: 3                    =     3.000000 <-- INTEGER
  PROD up to p=  3: 6                    =     6.000000 <-- INTEGER
  PROD up to p=  5: 9                    =     9.000000 <-- INTEGER
  PROD up to p=  7: 12                   =    12.000000 <-- INTEGER
  PROD up to p= 11: 72/5                 =    14.400000
  PROD up to p= 13: 84/5                 =    16.800000
  PROD up to p= 17: 189/10               =    18.900000
  PROD up to p= 19: 21                   =    21.000000 <-- 21 = 3*7 = FORBIDDEN NUMBER
  PROD up to p= 23: 252/11               =    22.909091
  PROD up to p= 29: 270/11               =    24.545455
  PROD up to p= 31: 288/11               =    26.181818
  PROD up to p= 37: 304/11               =    27.636364
  PROD up to p= 41: 1596/55              =    29.018182
  PROD up to p= 43: 152/5                =    30.400000
  PROD up to p= 47: 3648/115             =    31.721739
  PROD up to p= 53: 49248/1495           =    32.941806
  PROD up to p= 59: 295488/8671          =    34.077730
  PROD up to p= 61: 1526688/43355        =    35.213655
  PROD up to p= 67: 17302464/476905      =    36.280735
  PROD up to p= 71: 622888704/16691675   =    37.317328

FACTORIZATION ANALYSIS
----------------------------------------

  PROD(p+1)/(p-1) for p=2,3,5,7,11,13,17,19
  Numerator:   PROD(p+1) = 3*4*6*8*12*14*18*20
             = 34836480
  Denominator: PROD(p-1) = 1*2*4*6*10*12*16*18
             = 1658880
  Ratio: 34836480/1658880 = 21 (with remainder 0)

TELESCOPING STRUCTURE
----------------------------------------

  Write p+1 and p-1 for each prime:
    p= 2: (p+1)/(p-1) = 3/1
    p= 3: (p+1)/(p-1) = 4/2
    p= 5: (p+1)/(p-1) = 6/4
    p= 7: (p+1)/(p-1) = 8/6
    p=11: (p+1)/(p-1) = 12/10
    p=13: (p+1)/(p-1) = 14/12
    p=17: (p+1)/(p-1) = 18/16
    p=19: (p+1)/(p-1) = 20/18

  Key observation: many factors appear in BOTH numerator and denominator.
  The massive cancellation leaves only the 'boundary' factors.

  Prime factorization of numerator PROD(p+1):
    2^12    3^5    5^1    7^1
  Prime factorization of denominator PROD(p-1):
    2^12    3^4    5^1

  After cancellation:
  Numerator: 3^1 7^1 = 21
  Denominator: = 1
  Result: 21/1 = 21

