  Integer values of the prime Cayley product:
    Up to p=2: product = 3
    Up to p=3: product = 6
      = 2*3
    Up to p=5: product = 9
      = 3*3
    Up to p=7: product = 12
      = 2*2*3
    Up to p=19: product = 21
      = 3 * 7 = the two FORBIDDEN-adjacent primes
      = 3*7

CONNECTION TO MERTENS' THEOREM
----------------------------------------

  Mertens' theorem: PROD_{p<=x} (1-1/p) ~ e^{-gamma}/ln(x)
  where gamma = Euler-Mascheroni constant = 0.5772...

  Our product: PROD_{p<=x} (p+1)/(p-1) = PROD (1+1/p)/(1-1/p)
  = PROD(1+1/p) / PROD(1-1/p)
  = [PROD(1+1/p)] * [ln(x) * e^gamma + O(1)]

  By Mertens: PROD(1+1/p) ~ C * ln(x) as well (with different C).
  So our product ~ C' * ln(x)^2 asymptotically.

  At p=113: product/4.7274^2 = 2.067996
